Widget.qml and Avatar.qml here are derived from Rakabot's files, which are in
turn derived from omabot's. The visual design, the avatar rendering (shapes,
colour handling, eyes, expressions, entrance and gesture flourishes) and the
bar/panel layout come from that lineage; what is new for Herbot is the data
layer, which reads a local Hermes install instead of a hosted chat service, and
the actions, which open Hermes and deliver into a bot's canonical chat.

Modified files
--------------
Widget.qml and Avatar.qml are changed versions of the files in Rakabot. Section
4(b) of the licence asks for a prominent notice of modification, so each of
those files carries a comment at the top naming the original, the licence and
what changed. In short: the roster is read from the local Hermes profile
metadata and session store instead of Rakazo's RPC API, the palette and shape
list are Hermes' (`ui_meta['hermes-bots']`), the status wording is Hermes'
("waiting on you" is the backend's own read watermark), and the actions open
Hermes Desktop or send into a bot's canonical Bot Chat.

New files, not derived from that lineage: bin/hermbot-watch,
bin/hermbot-open, bin/hermbot-send, manifest.json, README.md,
CHANGELOG.md, NOTICE, docs/, scripts/ and tests/.

